            <ArticleTitle>[Spontaneous rupture of a pancreatic pseudocyst into the descending colon].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2173-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 50-year-old male with nausea and upper abdominal pain was hospitalised. After five days, lower gastrointestinal bleeding occurred. Computed tomography (CT) revealed a pancreatic pseudocyst. Coloscopic biopsy indicated fistulisation of a pancreatic pseudocyst into the descending colon. The patient was successfully treated nonoperatively, using only antibiotics.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
